    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is fully satisfied and the suite is green (6 tests, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement \u2014 all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail` \u2014 is implemented in this codebase, and I verified it end-to-end.\n\n**How it works.** Every rejection flows through OfficeFloor escalation handlers under `src/main/java/.../rest/escalation/`, one per business-rule exception. There are no rejection responses anywhere else (I grepped the functions for inline `BAD_REQUEST`/`CONFLICT`/`TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`/`ResponseEntity<String>` and found none). Each handler builds its body through a single shared helper, `ProblemDetails.build(ex, status, detail)`, which sets `type` (`about:blank`), `title` (exception simple name), `status`, `detail`, plus a `timestamp` and a `schemaValidationErrors` placeholder \u2014 keeping the shared shape in one place rather than duplicated per handler:\n\n- **400** \u2014 `MissingOwnerFields`, `InvalidTelephone`, `InvalidEmail`, `InvalidPostcode`, `DisposableEmailDomain`, `FutureRegistrationDate`, `MethodArgumentNotValid` (adds `schemaValidationErrors`).\n- **409** \u2014 `DuplicateIdentity`, `CityAtCapacity`.\n- **429** \u2014 `DailyLimitReached`.\n\nEach sends `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` with the matching status, and Spring's `ProblemDetail` message converter emits `application/problem+json` (HTTP codes unchanged).\n\n**Verification.** The new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` passes (asserts content type `application/problem+json` and `$.status == 400`). I also ran a throwaway test that dumped a real 400 body to confirm all four required members are present, then removed it:\n\n```json\n{\"detail\":\"The request is missing one or more required owner fields\",\"instance\":\"/api/owners\",\"status\":400,\"title\":\"MissingOwnerFieldsException\",\"type\":\"about:blank\",...}\n```\n\nNo code changes were needed \u2014 the existing implementation already meets the spec, and I confirmed the full suite passes.",
